```

**Loud judgment call:** If Computer Motion is read as Wang’s company that Duggan later ran (inherited), this row’s hit would move to Pharmacyclics (FY2011 $8.2M already above the 2011 bar **$6,986,920**; FY2012 $82.0M). I did not quietly pick the famous 2015 sale.

**Uncertain:** a1 Wikipedia says 1944 or 1945; a2 1962 is implied by “turned 18 in 1962, enrolled at UCSB”, not a diploma date.

